@.str.53 = private unnamed_addr constant [1487 x i8] c"\0A\0A# Examples\0A\0A* Bundle Hello:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix bundle nixpkgs#hello\0A  # ./hello\0A  Hello, world!\0A  ```\0A\0A* Bundle a specific version of Nix:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix bundle github:NixOS/nix/e3ddffb27e5fc37a209cfd843c6f7f6a9460a8ec\0A  # ./nix --version\0A  nix (Nix) 2.4pre20201215_e3ddffb\0A  ```\0A\0A* Bundle a Hello using a specific bundler:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix bundle --bundler github:NixOS/bundlers#toDockerImage nixpkgs#hello\0A  # docker load < hello-2.10.tar.gz\0A  # docker run hello-2.10:latest hello\0A  Hello, world!\0A  ```\0A\0A# Description\0A\0A`nix bundle`, by default, packs the closure of the [*installable*](./nix.md#installables) into a single\0Aself-extracting executable. See the [`bundlers`\0Ahomepage](https://github.com/NixOS/bundlers) for more details.\0A\0A> **Note**\0A>\0A> This command only works on Linux.\0A\0A# Flake output attributes\0A\0AIf no flake output attribute is given, `nix bundle` tries the following\0Aflake output attributes:\0A\0A* `bundlers.<system>.default`\0A\0AIf an attribute *name* is given, `nix bundle` tries the following flake\0Aoutput attributes:\0A\0A* `bundlers.<system>.<name>`\0A\0A# Bundlers\0A\0AA bundler is specified by a flake output attribute named\0A`bundlers.<system>.<name>`. It looks like this:\0A\0A```nix\0Abundlers.x86_64-linux = rec {\0A  identity = drv: drv;\0A\0A  blender_2_79 = drv: self.packages.x86_64-linux.blender_2_79;\0A\0A  default = identity;\0A};\0A```\0A\0AA bundler must be a function that accepts an arbitrary value (typically a\0Aderivation or app definition) and returns a derivation.\0A\0A\00", align 1
